Found by the grep asked for in #10: second occurrence of the "raw address
for a typed pointer out-param" pattern.

t/16-config.t:29-33

    my $name_out_buf = "\0" x 256;
    my ($name_out) = scalar_to_buffer($name_out_buf);
    my $rc_get = Git::Libgit2::FFI::git_config_get_string( $name_out, $config, "user.name" );
    ok( $rc_get < 0 || $rc_get == 0, "git_config_get_string returned (rc=" . $rc_get . ")" );

git_config_get_string is attached as [ "string*", "git_config", "string" ].
FFI::Platypus passes NULL when a non-ref is handed to a pointer-to-native
param -- proven by calling git_libgit2_version (int*, int*, int*), which does
not NULL-check its args, with a raw scalar_to_buffer address: segfault,
exit 139. So libgit2 never sees $name_out and the 256-byte buffer is dead
weight.

Two problems, neither fixed under #10 because the fix is not mechanical:

1. `rc < 0 || rc == 0` is true for every value libgit2 can return. The
   assertion cannot fail. Actual rc today is -1.
2. The out-param -- the only place the config value lands -- is never
   inspected. The test proves nothing beyond "it does not segfault".

Why it is not a one-line ref swap: the comment above it states that reading
back from the same config handle after git_config_set_string is not safe in
libgit2 1.5.x, which is why the sibling git_config_get_bool coverage right
below reads off a git_config_snapshot. Making this assertion real means
moving the read onto the snapshot path and asserting "Test User" -- deciding
what the test is for, not fixing a typo.

Suggested shape (mirror the get_bool block directly below):

    check_rc git_config_snapshot( \my $snap, $config );
    is( git_config_get_string( \my $name, $snap, "user.name" ), 0, ... );
    is( $name, "Test User", ... );
    git_config_free($snap);

and drop the scalar_to_buffer buffer entirely. Verify falsifiability by
mutating the expected string before calling it done.
Fixed in t/16-config.t (uncommitted, working tree).

Checked the premise first: the old comment claimed read-after-write on a
live config handle is "unsafe in libgit2 1.5.x". It is not a stability
issue, it is a hard API rule and libgit2 says so out loud -- on 1.5.1,
git_config_get_string against the live handle returns -1 with
"get_string called on a live config object" (klass 7, GIT_ERROR_CONFIG),
because the out-param borrows storage owned by the config object. So the
snapshot detour is required, not merely preferred, and the comment now
states that.

What replaced the tautology:
- isnt($rc_live, 0)   -- live handle refuses get_string
- like(Error->last($rc_live)->message, qr/live config object/)
- is($rc_get, 0)      -- get_string on a git_config_snapshot
- is($name, "Test User") -- the value actually written above
The scalar_to_buffer buffer and the now-unused FFI::Platypus::Buffer import
are gone. get_bool block below untouched (keeps its own snapshot).

Falsifiability proven by mutation (each on a scratch copy, run, reverted):
- write "Mutated User" instead of "Test User" -> not ok 5
- read user.email instead of user.name       -> not ok 5
- read off $config instead of $name_snap     -> not ok 4, not ok 5
- flip isnt->is on the live-handle rc        -> not ok 2
- expect a different error message           -> not ok 3

